# Schema of the box model (reference/common/structure.md).
# First the elements, then the reusable rules (Styles), the groups (Box, Typography,
# Break) and finally the properties.
# Each name has a single definition in the whole namespace: the Width of Page and the one of Box are
# the same node.
Schema (@stxt.schema): dev.stxt.pdf
	Description: Documents of stxt-pdf, the layout and PDF generation engine. Lengths are in points (12) or in millimeters (12mm). Manual in docs/en/manual and complete reference in docs/en/reference.

	# Elements

	Node: Document
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Box document: the medium (the one of the sections that do not declare their own), the title and the language (required), the subject, the author and the keywords (optional), the reusable rules (also the base typography, with For element: Document), the Page overlay of all the sections and one or more Section with the content, in order.
		Children:
			Child: Page
				Min: 1
				Max: 1
			Child: Title
				Min: 1
				Max: 1
			Child: Subject
				Max: 1
			Child: Author
				Max: 1
			Child: Keywords
				Max: 1
			Child: Language
				Min: 1
				Max: 1
			Child: Styles
				Max: 1
			Child: Page overlay
			Child: Section
				Min: 1
	Node: Page
		Type: GROUP
		Description: The page: its size, with Paper (and Orientation) or with Width and Height, and its margins, mirrored on the even pages with Mirror margins. It defines the page area, which is the initial reference container.
		Children:
			Child: Paper
				Max: 1
			Child: Orientation
				Max: 1
			Child: Width
				Max: 1
			Child: Height
				Max: 1
			Child: Margin
				Max: 1
			Child: Mirror margins
				Max: 1
	Node: Section
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Independent part of the document: it starts a new page and has its own Page (which inherits from the document by groups), its own Page overlay, its own page numbering and its footnote numbering. It contains the in-flow elements, the positioned ones and the Footnote.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Page
				Max: 1
			Child: Page numbering
				Max: 1
			Child: Page number format
				Max: 1
			Child: First number
				Max: 1
			Child: Inherit page overlays
				Max: 1
			Child: Begin on
				Max: 1
			Child: Footnote numbering
				Max: 1
			Child: Footnote number format
				Max: 1
			Child: Figure numbering
				Max: 1
			Child: Trim margins
				Max: 1
			Child: Block
			Child: Stack
			Child: Grid
			Child: Text
			Child: Paragraph
			Child: Heading 1
			Child: Heading 2
			Child: Heading 3
			Child: Heading 4
			Child: Heading 5
			Child: Heading 6
			Child: List
			Child: Markdown
			Child: Table of contents
			Child: Image
			Child: Barcode
			Child: Figure
			Child: Table
			Child: Columns
			Child: Frame
			Child: Overlay
			Child: Page overlay
			Child: Footnote
	Node: Block
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Box that stacks its children vertically (block flow). With Side, a side box: it goes to one side and the text of the siblings that follow it runs beside it.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Isolate margins
				Max: 1
			Child: Trim margins
				Max: 1
			Child: Rotate
				Max: 1
			Child: Side
				Max: 1
			Child: Below side boxes
				Max: 1
