				Max: 1
			Child: Vertical
				Max: 1
			Child: Line distribution
				Max: 1
			Child: Split items
				Max: 1
			Child: Item
			Child: Overlay
			Child: Page overlay
	Node: Grid
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Grid container: places its items (Area) in a grid of rows and columns.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Column sizes
				Max: 1
			Child: Row sizes
				Max: 1
			Child: Gap
				Max: 1
			Child: Area map
				Max: 1
			Child: Fill order
				Max: 1
			Child: Horizontal
				Max: 1
			Child: Vertical
				Max: 1
			Child: Split rows
				Max: 1
			Child: Area
			Child: Overlay
			Child: Page overlay
	Node: Text
		Type: INLINE
		Description: Standalone text, not a paragraph of the content: a label, a figure, a line of a header, the pieces of a heading. The text goes in the value (one line) or in Content (a block), without blank lines unless it is preformatted.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Content
				Max: 1
			Child: Rotate
				Max: 1
			Child: Below side boxes
				Max: 1
	Node: Paragraph
		Type: INLINE
		Description: A paragraph of the content, which For element: Paragraph rules style separately from standalone texts. A single paragraph: no blank lines in Content. With Drop cap, its first letter is a drop cap.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Content
				Max: 1
			Child: Rotate
				Max: 1
			Child: Below side boxes
				Max: 1
			Child: Drop cap
				Max: 1
	Node: Heading 1
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Level 1 heading: a block with one or more Text. It appears in the PDF bookmarks and the engine avoids breaking inside it and after it.
