	Node: Footnote
		Type: GROUP
		Description: A footnote: the content of a note that the engine places at the bottom of the page where the text calls it with [^id] (in a text with Markup: markdown or in a Markdown), under a rule, numbered in the order of the calls. Its Id is the name the call uses; it is written anywhere in its section and takes no space there. It starts with a Paragraph, a Text or a Markdown paragraph, which gets the number; no headings or images. Every note is called exactly once and every call has its note.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Min: 1
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Paragraph
			Child: Text
			Child: Markdown
			Child: List
			Child: Table
			Child: Block
	Node: Frame
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Frame: a block in its place in the flow that can be shifted with Offset without moving its siblings. It is the reference of the Overlay it contains.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Isolate margins
				Max: 1
			Child: Trim margins
				Max: 1
			Child: Offset
				Max: 1
			Child: Layer
				Max: 1
			Child: Rotate
				Max: 1
			Child: Rotate origin
				Max: 1
			Child: Opacity
				Max: 1
			Child: Block
			Child: Stack
			Child: Grid
			Child: Text
			Child: Paragraph
			Child: Heading 1
			Child: Heading 2
			Child: Heading 3
			Child: Heading 4
