			Child: Figure
			Child: Table
			Child: Columns
			Child: Frame
			Child: Overlay
			Child: Page overlay
			Child: Footnote

	Node: Markdown
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Content in Markdown (headings, paragraphs, lists, GFM tables, code blocks and, inline, **bold**, *italic*, ++underline++, ~~strikethrough~~, `code` and [links](target)), which is translated into Heading, Paragraph, List, Table and Text. A block.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Bullet markers
				Max: 1
			Child: Number markers
				Max: 1
			Child: Table column sizes
				Max: 1
			Child: Below side boxes
				Max: 1
			Child: Content
				Min: 1
				Max: 1
	Node: Table of contents
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Automatic table of contents: one entry per heading of the levels in Levels or, with Entries, per figure or per table (the Figure elements of that counter), in document order, with its title, a leader and the page. A block; the entries are styled with the For element rules 'TOC 1' to 'TOC 6' (those of figures and tables, 'TOC 1').
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Entries
				Max: 1
			Child: Levels
				Max: 1
			Child: Leader
				Max: 1
	Node: Figure
		Type: GROUP
		Description: A figure with a caption: exactly one element (an Image, a Barcode, a Table or a Block) and its Caption, below it (above a Table) or where Caption position says. A block that is not split across pages (a Table inside is, with the caption on its first or last part). It is numbered with the counter of the figures or, with a Table inside, of the tables (Figure counter changes it): the number, or its Number label, goes before the caption, {number of: id} gives it and a Table of contents with Entries: figures or tables lists it. Numbered: false in its Typography, or in a rule that reaches it, leaves it without a number. The image inside carries its Alt; with a Block, the Figure carries its own.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Alt
				Max: 1
			Child: Caption position
				Max: 1
			Child: Figure counter
				Max: 1
			Child: In table of contents
				Max: 1
			Child: Side
				Max: 1
			Child: Below side boxes
				Max: 1
			Child: Caption
				Min: 1
				Max: 1
			Child: Image
			Child: Barcode
			Child: Table
			Child: Block
	Node: Caption
		Type: INLINE
		Description: The caption of a Figure: a text, in the value (one line) or in Content (a block), that goes above or below the content of the figure, with the number of the figure before it. It inherits the Typography of the Figure, and For element: Caption styles all the captions.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Content
				Max: 1
	Node: Image
		Type: INLINE
		Description: PNG, JPEG, SVG or PDF image from the images/ folder of the resources; the value is its path, relative to images/ (logos/acme.png). A box without children with the size and proportions of the file (of a PDF, of its page); it does not break across pages. With Side, the text that follows it runs beside it.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Alt
				Max: 1
			Child: Fit
				Max: 1
			Child: Opacity
				Max: 1
			Child: PDF page
				Max: 1
			Child: Rotate
				Max: 1
			Child: Side
				Max: 1
			Child: Below side boxes
				Max: 1
	Node: Barcode
		Type: INLINE
		Description: QR code or barcode that the engine generates from its data, in the Barcode format qr (by default), data-matrix, gs1-data-matrix, pdf417, code-128, gs1-128 or ean-13. The data goes in the value (Barcode: https://example.com/verify/1234) or, if it has several lines, in a Content >> block, one of the two. It is laid out as an Image: its natural size comes from its modules (0.5 mm in a QR code and a Data Matrix; 0.33 mm by 1 mm in a PDF417; 0.33 mm by 22.85 mm in the barcodes of one row), with the quiet zone (Quiet zone) included; a QR code, a Data Matrix and a PDF417 are drawn whole and centered, and the barcodes of one row are stretched to the box. Readable text puts the data as text under the bars of a barcode of one row. Alt is required. The modules have the Color of the Typography and the background is that of the Box; of its Typography, only Color is allowed and, with Readable text, also Font, Size, Bold, Weight and Italic, those of that text.
		Children:
			Child: Id
				Max: 1
			Child: Style
				Max: 1
			Child: Link
				Max: 1
			Child: Box
				Max: 1
			Child: Typography
				Max: 1
			Child: Break
				Max: 1
			Child: Alt
				Max: 1
			Child: Barcode format
				Max: 1
			Child: Error correction
				Max: 1
			Child: Quiet zone
				Max: 1
			Child: Readable text
				Max: 1
			Child: Rotate
				Max: 1
			Child: Side
				Max: 1
			Child: Below side boxes
				Max: 1
			Child: Content
				Max: 1

	# Reusable rules

	Node: Styles
		Type: GROUP
		Description: Reusable rules: default properties of the elements of a type, with a named style or with an Id, and the colors with a name (Named color). It is a child of Document or the root of a separate styles document, which is passed along with the document and ranks below it.
		Children:
			Child: Named color
			Child: For element
			Child: For style
			Child: For id
			Child: For column
	Node: Named color
		Type: INLINE
		Description: Color with a name: the name and the color separated by a space (Named color: brand #12315A). The name, in lowercase letters and digits with words joined by hyphens, is then written wherever a color goes (Color, Border color, Background, also inside linear, and Separator color). If the document and the separate styles document declare the same name, the document wins.
	Node: For element
		Type: INLINE
		Description: Rule for all the elements of a type; the value is its name (Text, Block, Heading 1...), one generated by the engine (Code block, Block quote and Divider, the code blocks, the block quotes and the horizontal rules of a Markdown; TOC 1 to 6, the entries of a Table of contents; Footnote area, the area of the notes at the bottom of the page), a position within a table (Header cell, Body cell, Footer cell, Odd row cell, Even row cell) or Document, which only accepts Typography and is the typography that all boxes inherit. Besides the groups, it accepts the properties of how an element looks and distributes its content (Gap, Column sizes, Fit, Marker...) that the element of its type can declare; Grow, Shrink and Base size are those of the Item that wraps the element. A For element, For style or For column written inside it is a nested rule: it applies to the elements it names that are inside an element this rule applies to.
