	# Document

	Node: Title
		Description: Title of the document: the one the PDF viewer shows. Required.
	Node: Subject
		Description: What the document is about, in a sentence: the subject of the PDF, which the viewer shows in the document properties and which document managers and search engines index. Optional.
	Node: Author
		Description: Who writes the document: the person or the organization that the PDF names as its author, which the viewer shows in the document properties. Optional.
	Node: Keywords
		Description: Keywords of the document, separated by commas: the keywords of the PDF, which the viewer shows in the document properties and which document managers and search engines index. None empty. Optional.
	Node: Language
		Description: Language, as a BCP 47 tag (es, en-US, ca...). In Document, the one of the content and of the tagged PDF (required). In Typography, the one of a box whose text is in another language (inherited): a screen reader reads it (Lang of the tagged PDF) and it sets the letter rules of Case. Not valid in For element: Document, which uses the one of Document.

	# Element

	Node: Id
		Description: Identifier for dumps, tests, messages and For id rules. Unique in the document.
	Node: Style
		Description: Named styles of the element, separated by spaces: the For style rules with those names apply to it. In a Row, to each of its cells.
	Node: Link
		Description: Target the whole box leads to when clicked: https://..., http://..., mailto:... or #id (a box of the document). It does not change its appearance.
	Node: In table of contents
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the heading, or the Figure, has an entry in the tables of contents (Table of contents). By default, true. With false a heading is still a heading (structure, bookmark and hierarchy) but it is not listed: the title of the cover or the one of the table of contents itself; a Figure keeps its number and is not listed.
	Node: Isolate margins
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the box isolates the margins of its children: with true, those of the first and the last stay inside and do not merge with its own. By default, false.
	Node: Trim margins
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Which of the margins that touch the box from inside it drops: top, the top margin of its first child; bottom, the bottom margin of its last child; both, the two of them; none (by default), neither. With them go those of their own first and last children that would merge with them. A dropped margin is not applied: it neither stays inside the box nor comes out of it.
		Values:
			Value: none
			Value: both
			Value: top
			Value: bottom
	Node: Offset
		Description: Top, right, bottom, left (1 to 4 values). In a Frame, how far the box is shifted from its place in the flow. In an Overlay or a Page overlay, the distance from each edge of its reference container to the box; auto leaves that side free.
	Node: Layer
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Stacking order within its context: the lower ones are painted first, the negative ones beneath the content in flow. Without it, the box is painted in document order, like Layer: 0.
	Node: Pages
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Pages on which a Page overlay appears, counting from 1 within its scope (those of the document if it is a Page overlay of Document, those of the section if it is of a Section): all, every page; first, only the first; not-first, all but the first; odd, the odd ones; even, the even ones; last, only the last.
		Values:
			Value: all
			Value: first
			Value: not-first
			Value: odd
			Value: even
			Value: last
	Node: Page numbering
		Type: ENUM
		Description: How a Section numbers its pages with {page} and {pages}: continue (by default) follows the document counter, restart goes back to 1 and none neither numbers them nor advances the counter (a cover). {pages} is the last number of the page sequence, which starts at each restart.
		Values:
			Value: continue
			Value: restart
			Value: none
	Node: Page number format
		Type: ENUM
		Description: How the page numbers of a Section are written: decimal (1, by default), lower-alpha (a), upper-alpha (A), lower-roman (i) or upper-roman (I), in {page}, {pages}, {page of: id}, the tables of contents and the viewer. Not valid with Page numbering: none.
		Values:
			Value: decimal
			Value: lower-alpha
			Value: upper-alpha
			Value: lower-roman
			Value: upper-roman
	Node: Inherit page overlays
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the Section carries the Page overlay of the Document. By default, true; with false only its own appear (a cover without a footer).
	Node: Mirror margins
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the even physical pages swap the left and right margins of Margin, for double-sided printing: Margin is that of the odd pages, the right-hand ones. By default, false. A Section inherits it together with Margin. With equal left and right margins it has no effect and is an error.
	Node: Begin on
		Type: ENUM
		Description: On which physical page a Section starts: any (by default), on the next one; odd, on an odd one, the right-hand one when printing double-sided. If it does not fall there, the previous section ends with a blank page, which counts for the number but does not print it or carry the Page overlay. Not valid in the first section.
		Values:
			Value: any
			Value: odd
	Node: Footnote numbering
		Type: ENUM
		Description: How a Section numbers its footnotes: continue (by default) follows the counter of the document and restart goes back to 1.
		Values:
			Value: continue
			Value: restart
	Node: Figure numbering
		Type: ENUM
		Description: How a Section numbers its figures and its tables with a caption: continue (by default) follows the counters of the document (1, 2, 3) and chapter starts again in each chapter and writes its number first (2.3).
		Values:
			Value: continue
			Value: chapter
	Node: Footnote number format
		Type: ENUM
		Description: How the footnotes of a Section are numbered, in the call and in the note: decimal (1, by default), lower-alpha (a), upper-alpha (A), lower-roman (i), upper-roman (I) or symbols (*, †, ‡, §, and then doubled).
		Values:
			Value: decimal
			Value: lower-alpha
			Value: upper-alpha
			Value: lower-roman
			Value: upper-roman
			Value: symbols
	Node: Rotate
		Type: NUMBER
		Description: Rotation of the box, in degrees clockwise (from -360 to 360, without 0). In Block, Text, Paragraph, Image and Barcode, which are in flow, it rotates about its center and the box takes the rectangle that encloses it rotated; without Width, it measures its content without breaking lines. In Frame, Overlay and Page overlay it rotates when painting, around Rotate origin, and does not change the layout. What is rotated must fit on the page and does not break across pages.
	Node: Rotate origin
		Description: Point around which the border box rotates with Rotate: one or two keywords out of top, bottom, left, right and center (top left, bottom...), or two measures from its top left corner, as lengths or as a percentage of its width and its height (20 50%). By default, center.
	Node: Opacity
		Description: How opaque the box is painted, with everything it contains, as a percentage from 0% to 100% (Opacity: 15%): what lies beneath shows through it. With 100% the box is opaque, as without it, and with 0% nothing of it is seen. In an Image, the image with the background and the border of its box; in a Frame, an Overlay and a Page overlay, the box with its content, painted as a whole: what overlaps inside does not show through. Painting only: it does not change the layout. Without it, the box is opaque; the opacity of a single color goes in the color (#RRGGBBAA).
	Node: Side
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Side box: an Image, a Barcode or a Block (with Width or Max width) in block flow that goes to the left or to the right of its container, at its place in the flow, and the text of the siblings that follow it shortens its lines beside it; its Margin is the separation. A sibling that is not text (a Table, a Stack, a List) goes below it. It is not split across pages: if it does not fit, it moves to the next page with the first line that runs beside it. Not on an item of a Stack or a Grid, nor on a cell.
		Values:
			Value: left
			Value: right
	Node: Below side boxes
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the box goes below the side boxes (Side) before it, instead of running beside them. By default, false. Without a side box before it, it is an error.
	Node: Drop cap
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Drop cap of a Paragraph: its first letter is taken out of the text and set, in the font of the paragraph, at the size whose capitals are as tall as this number of lines (from 2 to 5), at the left of them. Not in a preformatted Paragraph.
	Node: Paper
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Named paper size of the medium, in portrait: A3 (297 × 420 mm), A4 (210 × 297 mm), A5 (148 × 210 mm), A6 (105 × 148 mm), B4 (250 × 353 mm), B5 (176 × 250 mm), Letter (612 × 792 pt) or Legal (612 × 1008 pt). It is not declared with Width or Height.
		Values:
			Value: A3
			Value: A4
			Value: A5
			Value: A6
			Value: B4
			Value: B5
			Value: Letter
			Value: Legal
	Node: Orientation
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Orientation of the paper of Paper: portrait (by default) or landscape, which swaps the width and the height.
		Values:
			Value: portrait
			Value: landscape
	Node: Content
		Type: BLOCK
		Description: Block text. A single line break counts as a space; a blank line is an error, except in a preformatted Text (Preformatted: keep or wrap). In a Barcode, the data, with its lines as they are.

	# Box

	Node: Width
		Description: Width of the border box (in Page, of the page).
	Node: Height
		Description: Height of the border box (in Page, of the page; in a Marker image, of the image, a positive length).
	Node: Min width
		Description: Minimum width.
	Node: Max width
		Description: Maximum width.
	Node: Min height
		Description: Minimum height.
	Node: Max height
		Description: Maximum height.
	Node: Aspect ratio
		Description: Width/height ratio (16/9 or a number): derives an auto axis from the other.
	Node: Margin
		Description: Margin: top, right, bottom, left (1 to 4 values).
	Node: Padding
		Description: Padding: top, right, bottom, left (1 to 4 values).
	Node: Border
		Description: Border width: top, right, bottom, left (1 to 4 values).
	Node: Border color
		Description: Border color: top, right, bottom, left (1 to 4 colors). By default, the Color of the text.
	Node: Border style
		Type: ENUM
		Description: How the border is drawn, the same on its four sides: solid (by default), dashed or dotted. The dashes are three times as long as the border is wide and the dots as wide as it, and they are spaced so that each side starts and ends with one. With Corner radius the pattern follows the curve, and the four sides of Border must be equally wide. With Merge borders, the line between two cells takes the style of the wider of their two borders. Painting only.
		Values:
			Value: solid
			Value: dashed
			Value: dotted
	Node: Corner radius
		Description: Rounded corners: top left, top right, bottom right, bottom left (1 to 4 values, number or %). Painting only: it rounds the background, the border and the clipping of an Image or a Barcode.
	Node: Background
		Description: Background, painted in the padding box: a color or a gradient linear(angle, color, color...).
	Node: Overflow
		Type: ENUM
		Description: What is done when what the box contains does not fit in it: error (by default) stops the conversion; shrink, only in a box with text (Text, Paragraph, a Cell with a value), reduces the Size of the text in steps of 0.5 pt until it fits, without going below Min size (if it still does not fit, it is an error); clip, only in a box without text inside, paints what sticks out of its padding box clipped (also the Overlay boxes inside) and does not split the box across pages.
		Values:
			Value: error
			Value: shrink
			Value: clip

	# Typography

	Node: Font
		Description: Font family, as declared by its TTF or OTF files in resources/fonts. Required in the text, own or inherited (also from Document).
	Node: Code font
		Description: Font family of the code (`code` in a text with Markup: markdown or in a Markdown, and the code blocks), as declared by its TTF or OTF files in resources/fonts; usually a monospaced one. Required if there is code, own or inherited.
	Node: Bold
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Bold: true is Weight: 700 and false, Weight: 400. By default, false. Not together with Weight in the same Typography.
	Node: Weight
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Weight of the font, from 100 (thin) to 900 (black) in steps of 100; the family needs a file with that weight in resources/fonts. By default, 400.
	Node: Italic
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Italic: the italic variant of the font. By default, false.
	Node: Size
		Description: Font size, a length. Required in the text, own or inherited (also from Document).
	Node: Min size
		Description: The smallest Size that Overflow: shrink may reduce the text to, a length. By default, 6. Inherited. In a box with Overflow: shrink it cannot be greater than Size.
	Node: Line height
		Description: Line height: a length, or a percentage (120%) relative to the Size.
	Node: Align
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Alignment of the lines.
		Values:
			Value: left
			Value: right
			Value: center
			Value: justify
	Node: Color
		Description: Color of the text.
	Node: Line breaking
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Line breaking of the text: simple (greedy, by default: each line is filled as much as it can) or optimal (Knuth-Plass, which chooses the breaks of the whole paragraph at once).
		Values:
			Value: simple
			Value: optimal
	Node: Hyphenate
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the line breaking may split a word at the end of a line with a hyphen, following the hyphenation patterns of the language of Language (the engine has them for es, ca, en-US, en-GB, de, fr, it, nl and pt; any other language is an error). By default, false. Inherited. A soft hyphen (U+00AD) in the text is always a break point, with or without Hyphenate, and is only painted where the word is split. So is a hyphen written between two letters or digits (REF-2026-0098): the line may end after it, with no other hyphen.
	Node: Break long words
		Type: ENUM
		Description: What is done with a part of a word that cannot be split further (it has no hyphen, written or soft, and Hyphenate does not split it) and is wider than a whole line of its box: never (by default; such a word is an error), new-line (it is cut at the last character that fits, with no hyphen, as many times as needed, and starts a line of its own) or same-line (cut the same way, it starts in the current line, after the words before it). Inherited. It is a last resort: a word that fits in a line of its own moves to the next line and is never cut. It does not change the narrowest width of the text. It has no effect on a preformatted text, where it is an error if the text itself declares it.
		Values:
			Value: never
			Value: new-line
			Value: same-line
	Node: First line indent
		Description: How much later the first line of the text starts, a length (without percentages): that line is that much shorter, and the text is aligned in what is left of it. By default, 0. Inherited: it is usually given with For element: Paragraph, which leaves headings and cells alone. Only the first line of the paragraph is indented: not the one after a forced line break, nor the first one of the part of a paragraph that goes on in another page or column. It can be negative (a hanging indent): the first line starts that much before the others, in the left Padding of its box, which has to be at least as large. It does not go in a Paragraph with Drop cap.
	Node: Markup
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Inline formatting of the text: none (by default; the text is literal) or markdown (interprets **bold**, *italic*, ++underline++, ~~strikethrough~~ and [links](target), with the CommonMark escapes; it does nothing inside a Markdown).
		Values:
			Value: none
			Value: markdown
	Node: Case
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Letter case of the text when painting it: none (by default), uppercase, lowercase or capitalize (the first letter of each word). The text of the document and the one in the PDF structure remain as written; the rules for each letter are those of the language of Language.
		Values:
			Value: none
			Value: uppercase
			Value: lowercase
			Value: capitalize
	Node: Letter spacing
		Description: Spacing between letters, a length, added to the advance of each character (also in line breaking and in justify); the last character of the line does not get it. It can be negative. By default, 0.
	Node: Small caps
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Small caps: lowercase letters are painted as uppercase at 80 % of the size. By default, false.
	Node: Position
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Position of a styled run on its line: normal (by default), superscript or subscript. A superscript and a subscript are painted at 70 % of the size, raised or lowered from the baseline, without changing the height of the line. Only in the For style rule of a styled run ([text]{name}): in a box it is an error.
		Values:
			Value: normal
			Value: superscript
			Value: subscript
	Node: Ligatures
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the text is measured and painted with the ligatures of the font (fi, fl). By default, true; with false, one glyph per character. Inherited. With Letter spacing other than 0 there are no ligatures. It only matters in the fonts that have them (IBM Plex Sans and Serif; Plex Mono does not).
	Node: Kerning
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the text is measured and painted with the kerning pairs of the font, which adjust the space between two letters (AV, To). By default, true. Inherited. The pairs come from the kern feature of the GPOS table or, in a font without it, from the kern table; a pair does not cross a space or the boundary between two runs. It does not change the text that is read or copied.
	Node: Preformatted
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Preformatted text: none (by default; spaces and line breaks count as a space), keep (keeps the spaces and line breaks, and does not break lines: one wider than the box is an error) or wrap (like keep, but breaks lines that are too wide between words). Preformatted lines are not justified.
		Values:
			Value: none
			Value: keep
			Value: wrap
	Node: Tab size
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: With Preformatted: keep or wrap, the width of a tab: each one leads to the next column that is a multiple of this number of characters. By default, 4.
	Node: Numbered
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the headings carry a number (1, 1.1, 1.1.1...), which is written before the title and is given by {number of: id}, the tables of contents and the PDF bookmarks. By default, false. Inherited: For element: Document turns it on in all of them, a For element rule in those of one level and, in the Typography of a heading, only in that one. Headings whose Numbered is false are neither numbered nor counted. A Figure is numbered by default, and only Numbered: false declared in it, or in a rule that reaches it, leaves it without a number.
	Node: Number format
		Type: ENUM
		Description: How the level number of a numbered heading, or the number of a Figure, is written: decimal (1, by default), lower-alpha (a), upper-alpha (A), lower-roman (i) or upper-roman (I). Each level of the full number is written with the one of its heading (II.a). Inherited.
		Values:
			Value: decimal
			Value: lower-alpha
			Value: upper-alpha
			Value: lower-roman
			Value: upper-roman
	Node: Number label
		Description: What is written before the title of a numbered heading, or before the caption of a numbered Figure, with {number} where the number goes (Number label: Annex {number}., Number label: Figure {number}.); without it, the number. Inherited.
	Node: Widows
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Minimum number of lines of a paragraph that move to the next page. By default, 2.
	Node: Orphans
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Minimum number of lines of a paragraph that stay at the end of a page. By default, 2.

	# Break

	Node: Before
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Break before the box: auto (by default) does not force it; page takes it to a new page and column, inside a Columns, to the next column.
		Values:
			Value: auto
			Value: page
			Value: column
	Node: After
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Break after the box: auto (by default) does not force it; page takes what follows to a new page and column, inside a Columns, to the next column.
		Values:
			Value: auto
			Value: page
			Value: column
	Node: Keep with next
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the box is kept on the same page as the next one: it avoids the break between the two (titles, labels). By default, false. With After: page or column, it is a contradiction.
	Node: Keep with previous
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the box is kept on the same page as the previous one: it avoids the break between the two. By default, false. With Before: page or column, it is a contradiction.
	Node: Keep together
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the box is kept whole: it avoids breaking it across pages. By default, false.
	Node: Edges
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Border and padding of a box broken across pages: open (by default) leaves them open at the break; closed closes them in each fragment, which carries its full border and padding.
		Values:
			Value: open
			Value: closed

	# Stack

	Node: Direction
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Main axis of a Stack, along which the items go one after another: horizontal (by default) or vertical.
		Values:
			Value: horizontal
			Value: vertical
	Node: Wrap items
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether the items that do not fit in a line go to the next one, so that they are distributed over several lines. By default, false.
	Node: Split items
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: With true (by default), a line of a Stack (in vertical, an item) that does not fit in what is left of the page is broken on that page, each item on its own; with false it moves whole to the next page, and is only broken if it does not fit on a whole page either.
	Node: Gap
		Description: Spacing: in Stack and Grid, one value, or two (rows columns); in Columns, one value, the gap between columns.
	Node: Line distribution
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Distribution of the lines in the container: at one of its sides (top or bottom in a horizontal Stack, whose lines go from top to bottom; left or right in a vertical one, whose lines go from left to right), center, justify (the first and the last at the edges), distribute (equal gaps, also at the edges) or stretch. Only with Wrap items: true.
		Values:
			Value: top
			Value: bottom
			Value: left
			Value: right
			Value: center
			Value: justify
			Value: distribute
			Value: stretch
	Node: Grow
		Description: Share of the leftover space that the item receives.
	Node: Shrink
		Description: Share of the shortfall that the item gives up, weighted by Base size.
	Node: Base size
		Description: Starting size of the item on the main axis.

	# Grid

	Node: Column sizes
		Description: Size of each column: one track per column.
	Node: Row sizes
		Description: Size of each row: one track per row.
	Node: Area map
		Type: TEXT
		Description: One row of the grid per line; names separated by spaces and . for empty cells.
	Node: Fill order
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Order of the automatic placement of a Grid: rows (by default) fills the rows one by one; columns, the columns.
		Values:
			Value: rows
			Value: columns
	Node: Split rows
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: With true (by default), a row of a Grid or a Table that does not fit in what is left of the page is broken on that page, each item on its own; with false it moves whole to the next page, and is only broken if it does not fit on a whole page either.
	Node: Merge borders
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Only in a Table (from a rule of Styles, the other boxes ignore it): with true, the border between two cells is drawn once, centered on the line between them, with the wider of their two borders (and its color); the outer border of the table goes inside it; with false, each cell paints its own border. True by default; a table none of whose cells has a border has nothing to merge.
	Node: Horizontal
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Horizontal alignment or distribution. In a Grid, the alignment of all the items in their area, and in an Area, that of one (left, right, center or stretch). In a Stack, if its main axis is the horizontal one, the distribution of the leftover space (left, right, center, justify or distribute); if not, the alignment of all the items (left, right, center or stretch). In an Item, the alignment of one, only if it is the cross axis of its Stack.
		Values:
			Value: left
			Value: right
			Value: center
			Value: stretch
			Value: justify
			Value: distribute
	Node: Vertical
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Vertical alignment or distribution, like Horizontal: in a Grid and in an Area, the alignment in the area; in a Stack, the distribution if its main axis is the vertical one and, if not, the alignment of the items; in an Item, the alignment of one, only if it is the cross axis of its Stack. baseline is only for the cross axis of a Stack with Direction: horizontal and its Item: the items are aligned by the baseline of their first line of text, and an item without text rests its bottom on it. In a Cell, where its content goes in the height its row leaves over, like the distribution of a vertical Stack: top (by default), center or bottom; the box of the cell stays stretched to its row.
		Values:
			Value: top
			Value: bottom
			Value: center
			Value: stretch
			Value: baseline
			Value: justify
			Value: distribute

	# List

	Node: Marker
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Marker of the items: bullet (•), dash (–) or none, an image (the Marker image of the list or of each item), or a numbering (1., a., A., i., I.; with Marker suffix: parenthesis, 1), a)...).
		Values:
			Value: bullet
			Value: dash
			Value: none
			Value: image
			Value: decimal
			Value: lower-alpha
			Value: upper-alpha
			Value: lower-roman
			Value: upper-roman
	Node: Marker suffix
		Type: ENUM
		Description: What follows the number in the markers of a numbered List: period (1., a.), the default, or parenthesis (1), a)). Only with a Marker that numbers.
		Values:
			Value: period
			Value: parenthesis
	Node: Marker image
		Type: INLINE
		Description: Image of the marker, with Marker: image, in the List (for all its items) or in a List item (its own, which replaces that of the list); the value is its path, relative to images/, as in an Image. As tall as the Size of the item unless it declares Height, as wide as its proportion gives, centered on the capitals of the first line of the item and followed by a space. With Alt it is read as a figure; without it, it is decorative.
		Children:
			Child: Alt
				Max: 1
			Child: Height
				Max: 1
	Node: First number
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Number a numbering starts with: that of the first item of a numbered list or, in a Section with Page numbering: restart, that of its first page. By default, 1.
	Node: Number
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Number of this item of a numbered list; the following ones continue from it.

	# Table

	Node: Span
		Description: Rows and columns the cell spans, in that order (1 1 by default): 1 3 spans three columns of its row.
	Node: Row header
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: The cell is the header of its row (the item of an invoice, the time of a timetable): in the tagged PDF it is a TH with Scope Row, and a screen reader announces it with each cell of the row. By default, false. Not valid in Header rows, whose cells are already column headers.
	Node: Column align
		Description: Alignment of each column of a Table (left, center, right or justify), one per column: it is the default value of its cells, which the Styles rules and what the cell declares override.

	# Columns

	Node: Column count
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Number of columns of a Columns (at least 1); with Min column width, the maximum.
	Node: Min column width
		Description: Minimum width of the columns: as many fit as the width allows, up to Column count if it is declared.
	Node: Separator
		Description: Width of the line between the columns of a Columns, centered in Gap, which must be at least as wide.
	Node: Separator color
		Description: Color of the line between columns. By default, the Color of the text.
	Node: Separator style
		Type: ENUM
		Description: How the line between columns is drawn: solid (by default), dashed or dotted, like Border style. Only with Separator.
		Values:
			Value: solid
			Value: dashed
			Value: dotted
	Node: Balance columns
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Distribution among the columns of a Columns: with true (by default) the columns of the last fragment are balanced; with false they are filled in order.

	# Image

	Node: Alt
		Description: Alternative text of an Image or a Barcode: with it, the image is a figure (Figure) of the tagged PDF; without it, an Image is decorative. A Barcode requires it, and so does the image of a Figure. In a Figure with a Block, the alternative text of the whole figure, required.
	Node: Fit
		Type: ENUM
		Description: How an Image fills its box if they have different proportions: inside (by default) fits whole and centered; crop fills the box, centered, and crops what is left over; stretch stretches it to the box and distorts it.
		Values:
			Value: inside
			Value: crop
			Value: stretch
	Node: PDF page
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Page drawn by an Image of a PDF, from 1 (by default, the first). In an image that is not a PDF, or a page the PDF does not have, it is an error.

	# Barcode

	Node: Barcode format
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Symbology of a Barcode: qr (by default), a QR code; data-matrix, a square Data Matrix; pdf417, a PDF417; code-128, printable ASCII characters, up to 80; ean-13, 12 digits (the check digit is added) or 13 (it is checked); gs1-128 and gs1-data-matrix, a Code 128 and a Data Matrix with GS1 data, a list of application identifiers in parentheses, each one before its value, as in (01)09501101530003(10)AB-123.
		Values:
			Value: qr
			Value: data-matrix
			Value: gs1-data-matrix
			Value: pdf417
			Value: code-128
			Value: gs1-128
			Value: ean-13
	Node: Error correction
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Error correction of a QR code, the part of its modules that can be damaged and it can still be read: low (7 %), medium (15 %, by default), quartile (25 %) or high (30 %). In another Barcode format, it is an error: a Data Matrix has its own, and a PDF417 takes the level its standard recommends for its data.
		Values:
			Value: low
			Value: medium
			Value: quartile
			Value: high
	Node: Quiet zone
		Type: INTEGER
		Description: Light modules on each side of a Barcode, which the reader needs around the code, from 0 to 40. By default, those of its standard: 4 in a QR code, 1 in a Data Matrix, 2 in a PDF417, 10 in a Code 128 and a GS1-128, and 11 on the left and 7 on the right in an EAN-13. They are part of its natural size, so in a box of a given size fewer modules of quiet zone give wider modules.
	Node: Readable text
		Type: BOOLEAN
		Description: Whether a barcode of one row (code-128, gs1-128 or ean-13) has its data as text under its bars, in the font, the size and the color of its Typography. By default, false. In an EAN-13 it is laid out as on a product: the first digit at the left of the bars, each of the others under its seven modules and the guard bars going down between them; in the others, one centered line (in a GS1-128, with the parentheses of its application identifiers). Its height is added to the natural height of the code and, in a box of a given height, taken from the bars. A text that does not fit under its bars is an error. In another Barcode format, it is an error.

	# Markdown

	Node: Bullet markers
		Description: Markers of the bulleted lists (-, *, +) of a Markdown, one per nesting level (the last one serves the deeper levels): bullet, dash or none.
	Node: Number markers
		Description: Markers of the numbered lists (1., 1)) of a Markdown, one per nesting level (the last one serves the deeper levels): decimal, lower-alpha, upper-alpha, lower-roman or upper-roman. A list written with 1) has Marker suffix: parenthesis.
	Node: Table column sizes
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Columns of the tables of a Markdown: equal, all of the same width (repeat(n, *)); auto, each according to its content (repeat(n, auto)).
		Values:
			Value: equal
			Value: auto

	# Figure

	Node: Caption position
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Where the Caption of a Figure goes: top, above its content, or bottom, below it. By default, bottom, and top in a Figure with a Table.
		Values:
			Value: top
			Value: bottom
	Node: Figure counter
		Type: ENUM
		Description: The counter a Figure is numbered with and the tables of contents that list it: figures or tables. By default, tables in a Figure with a Table and figures in the rest.
		Values:
			Value: figures
			Value: tables

	# Table of contents

	Node: Entries
		Type: ENUM
		Description: What a Table of contents lists: headings (by default), the headings of its Levels; figures or tables, the Figure elements numbered with that counter, with the text of their caption. With figures or tables, Levels has no effect and is an error.
		Values:
			Value: headings
			Value: figures
			Value: tables
	Node: Levels
		Description: Heading levels listed by a Table of contents with Entries: headings: the first and the last, from 1 to 6 (by default, 1 3).
	Node: Leader
		Type: ENUM
		Description: Leader between the title and the page of the entries of a Table of contents: dots (by default), line (a line) or none.
		Values:
			Value: dots
			Value: line
			Value: none
